WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.060
Speaker 1: Well, folks, we are not going to
be getting those Secret Service text messages.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.130
Many of you I know have been following this
story this week, anxiously awaiting yesterday,

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:14.849
Tuesday, when supposedly the text messages
deleted by the Secret Service after they were

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.300
told, don't delete these text messages, preserve
records.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:25.220
They are not going to be able to able to turn
them over to the January 6th committee investigating

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.500
the Trump riots.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.680
This is a really, really big deal.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.010
This really actually should be a major scandal.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.780
And I don't know if it's going to become one
as it seems.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.300
Even the Secret Service under Trump, which
we suspected, we talked about it at the time,

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:45.460
even the Secret Service under Trump, supposedly,
in theory, apolitical, has fallen fell under

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.739
the thumb of wacky Trumpism.

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:51.290
So let's reset the story.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:58.931
The January six committee subpoenaed some
U.S. Secret Service records because a government

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:06.180
watchdog found believed that the agency had
erased two important text messages from January

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.330
5th and January 6th, 2021.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:15.680
The Secret Service was told even if these
were deleted, you have to recover them.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.130
And there were conflicting and changing explanations
as to why the Secret Service didn't have them

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.130
first.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:26.380
It was something related to changes to the
pieces of equipment, elements of technology

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.390
that they were using.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.390
They did a phone migration.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:34.939
Well, it turns out that that phone migration
started after the request for these text messages.

00:01:34.939 --> 00:01:38.770
So it's all increasingly more and more fishy.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.060
And now we learn you're not going to get the
text messages.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.380
Washington Post report.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:49.290
Secret Service cannot okay, cannot recover
texts.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.790
No new details for the January six committee.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.650
The US Secret Service has determined it has
no new text messages to provide Congress relevant

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:02.960
to its January 6th investigation and that
any other texts its agents exchanged around

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.800
the time of the Trump riots were purged.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.800
Purged.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:12.930
Also, the National Archives sought more information
on the potential unauthorized deletion of

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.470
agency text messages.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:18.440
The US government's chief record keeper asked
Secret Service to report back within 30 days

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:23.580
about the deletion of records, including describing
what was purged and the circumstances of how

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.750
the documentation was lost.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.530
It's just gone, guys.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.730
And yes, it's as suspicious as a situation
as it sounds.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:39.700
It is amazing what you are unable to do when
you're determined not to do something.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.560
And I'm reminded of Donald Trump and his tax
records.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:50.099
Donald Trump was obviously, from day one,
determined never to publish his private tax

00:02:50.099 --> 00:02:51.099
records.

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:52.099
It was abundantly clear.

00:02:52.099 --> 00:02:56.850
And so first it was, well, I'm under audit,
as he like to say, from the IRS.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.840
And once the audits are complete.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.870
But wait, sir, which years are under audit?

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:02.870
Give us something.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.920
It can't be that every year of recent taxes.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.629
Well, I'm under audit.

00:03:06.629 --> 00:03:07.629
I'm under audit.

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:09.220
And my lawyers say, don't do it.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.220
Okay.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.220
So then after it.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.220
Well, no.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.220
And well, now it's reelection.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.220
It's four years later.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.060
You're not still being audited for those same
years, are you?

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.069
Well, I don't know.

00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:18.860
The American people don't care about that.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.020
He was determined not to publish his tax returns.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.230
And he didn't publish them.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:32.040
The Secret Service here was clearly determined
not to recover or provide or publicize or

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.349
deliver these text messages.

00:03:34.349 --> 00:03:35.960
And that's exactly what they're doing.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:43.489
So now we have at least a reasonable suspicion
that Secret Service was involved, complicit,

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.390
indifferent to what was going on on January
6th.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:53.500
Now, let's add to that add to our understanding
this seemingly strange data point.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.720
Mike Pence didn't want to get in the car with
Secret Service on that day.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.720
That's weird.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.440
But we didn't really know what to make of
it, at least not initially.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.010
It kind of doesn't make sense.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:09.560
Why wouldn't the if Secret Service comes to
the vice president and says, Mr. Vice President,

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.080
sir, we've got to get you out of here, it's
not safe.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.879
And Pence goes, I'm not going.

00:04:14.879 --> 00:04:17.120
I'm not getting in a car with you guys.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.150
That is strange.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.909
But it was sort of out of context initially.

00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:27.330
Do we now have a little bit more of the picture
where Secret Service here seemingly for what

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.749
appear to be political reasons?

00:04:28.749 --> 00:04:32.360
I mean, there's been no other explanation
given the explanations about technological

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.360
reasons shifted.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.089
So it was a data migration, it was new devices.

00:04:36.089 --> 00:04:38.990
It was these different things that none of
it makes sense.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:46.939
But what now does make some sense is the idea
that Pence knew what we are increasingly aware

00:04:46.939 --> 00:04:54.909
of, which is that even the Secret Service
was not infiltrated but taken over by Trump

00:04:54.909 --> 00:04:56.129
loyalists.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:05:01.689
If you think back to when Trump was in the
hospital with COVID and on day two, Trump

00:05:01.689 --> 00:05:08.330
insisted on going out for this joyride with
his mask on to wave to people around Walter

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.330
Reed Hospital.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.039
And we all said that's hugely irresponsible.

00:05:11.039 --> 00:05:16.099
He's stuffing a bunch of he's he's very sick
and he's stuffing Secret Service agents into

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:17.099
the vehicle.

00:05:17.099 --> 00:05:20.689
And we heard anecdotally, oh, some of the
Secret Service agents didn't like it.

00:05:20.689 --> 00:05:23.879
They were exposed a high rate of COVID among
them.

00:05:23.879 --> 00:05:25.789
Maybe most of them are actually okay with
it.

00:05:25.789 --> 00:05:31.149
I mean, at the end of the day, if it was Trump
loyalists handpicked, even within Secret Service

00:05:31.149 --> 00:05:34.949
to be around, maybe they thought it was cool
that he was going around and saying hi to

00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:35.949
the people.

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:39.509
So that's increasingly the picture we have
of Secret Service under Trump.

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:43.009
Now, separately, what's going on with Merrick
Garland?

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.369
Merrick Garland as attorney general.

00:05:45.369 --> 00:05:51.789
And so far he's shown no willingness, willingness
to really go after high level people potentially

00:05:51.789 --> 00:05:56.089
involved with criminality related to January
six, related to the post-election period.

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:57.179
What's going on at DOJ?

00:05:57.179 --> 00:05:58.789
We don't know.

00:05:58.789 --> 00:06:01.369
This is investigation worthy.

00:06:01.369 --> 00:06:06.139
The Secret Service should be investigated
over these deleted texts by the highest level,

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:07.970
and that would be as a federal agency.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.309
That would be by the Department of Justice.

00:06:10.309 --> 00:06:12.119
Is that going to happen?

00:06:12.119 --> 00:06:15.129
Is there any evidence Merrick Garland is willing
to do that?

00:06:15.129 --> 00:06:17.830
It's an extraordinarily suspicious timeline.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:23.899
Congress tells the Secret Service preserve
the documents from January five and six.

00:06:23.899 --> 00:06:25.340
On January 16th.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.759
It had only been ten days.

00:06:26.759 --> 00:06:28.830
January 16th, 2021.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.409
Congress says keep the documents.

00:06:31.409 --> 00:06:37.249
And then again, they say that on January 25th
and then two days later.

00:06:37.249 --> 00:06:41.349
This is now two weeks after being told keep
the records.

00:06:41.349 --> 00:06:47.259
The Secret Service starts a phone migration
and all of a sudden it's all gone and we can't

00:06:47.259 --> 00:06:48.399
get any of it.

00:06:48.399 --> 00:06:49.509
This is major news.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:51.520
This should be a major scandal.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:07:40.369
We will see where 

00:07:40.369 --> 00:08:06.009
it goes.

